Implemented **`DET.DATA.TABLE_HEADERS`** as a deterministic DOM check aligned with the catalog rule: data tables must use `<th scope>` or explicit `headers` associations.

### Source rule → measurable signals

From `deterministic-design-rules.md`: pass when visible data tables either:

1. Use `<th>` (or `role="columnheader"` / `role="rowheader"`) with valid `scope` (`col`, `row`, `colgroup`, `rowgroup`), or  
2. Every body `<td>` has a `headers` attribute pointing at header cell ids in the same table.

### What was added

**`design-rules/deterministic/generated/det-data-table-headers.check.js`**

- `collectTableHeadersReport(page)` — scans visible `<table>` elements with at least one visible `<td>`
- Skips layout tables (`role="presentation"`, hidden subtrees)
- Violations:
  - `no-header-cells` — no header cells and not all `td` have valid `headers`
  - `th-missing-scope` — header cells exist but lack `scope`, and not all `td` use `headers`
- `findingsFromTableHeadersReport()` / `run({ metrics, page, url })` — same pattern as `DET.CHART.ALT_SUMMARY` and `DET.DATA.COLOR_ONLY` (`metrics.tableHeadersReport` when precomputed)

**`design-rules/blender/rule-mappings.js`**

- Registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **implemented** with `area: accessibility`, `scoreDimension: accessibilitySemanticsMeta`, `priorityWeight: 7`, `defaultSeverity: major`

**`auditor-tests/det-data-table-headers.test.js`**

- Unit tests for findings helpers and `run()`

**`design-rules/registry.generated.json`**

- Rule marked **implemented** (18 implemented / 32 stub)

### Finding shape (backward compatible)

- `severity`: `major`
- `area`, `message`, `evidence` (`missing_table_headers issue=…`), `remediation`
- Optional `url=` on evidence when a URL is provided

